Hello List,
I have conducted a harbour porpoise behavioural study using a point trans=
ect
design.  I want to estimate the density and abundance based on the radial=

distances.=20=20

My problem is that my survey effort varied per point.  Based on what I've=

read I need to use a multiplier to scale the density/abundance estimates

accordingly.=20=20

I have created a column in my data that has the survey effort for each

point, and when I tell Distance that I would like to use a multiplier dur=

ing
the project set up, I selected the "Other" option and called it Survey
Effort.  Then I  get a column  in the global data layer called Survey
Effort, with a value of 1, which is incorrect.  How do I get Distance to
recognise the variable number of visits to each point?

Any insight into solving this problem is greatly appreciated.

Regards,
Anna Hall

